     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the estimate rings down under the force it drives\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<estimated position\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<feedback force\>\""}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[270]:= ",
 CellID->57325639,ExpressionUUID->"27508344-1169-d276-4d6f-1b2ea01da15c"],

Cell["\<\
The estimate rings down as the force pushes against it, the mechanical \
analogue of a shock absorber built from a measurement.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1374945886,ExpressionUUID->"52bd9efb-5696-d8d3-0242-17a56320aa39"],

Cell["\<\
How hard should the loop push? Sweep the gain and read the steady occupation \
off the exact Lyapunov balance:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->456950207,ExpressionUUID->"59d784c6-d1d1-3822-0fec-1da3e0658b08"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gainsCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "12", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"gainsCool", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"nUncCool", " ", "/@", " ", "gainsCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<feedback gain G\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<an optimal gain: too little leaves it warm, too much feeds \
noise back\>\""}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "2", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "nCool"}], "}"}]}], 
        "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", "97", "]"}], "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        "Dashed"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Last", "@", "gainsCool"}], ",", " ", "condFloorCool"}], 
          "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[271]:= ",
 CellID->1460592219,ExpressionUUID->"0af74c3d-c5cb-eb2b-3a8d-6666ec7fb671"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The occupation falls steeply from the heated open-loop value, reaches a \
minimum near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["G", "TI"], "\[TildeTilde]", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18e44c83-1c1f-43b5-489c-65ed95aa119f"],
 ", then rises again: beyond the optimum the loop feeds the estimate's own \
measurement noise back onto the oscillator, the imprecision-back-action \
tradeoff that caps every real feedback-cooling experiment. It never reaches \
the conditional floor (green): that would need a noiseless actuator acting on \
a perfectly known state."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1677337148,ExpressionUUID->"6026f33f-0f19-e769-11dd-eb79aaadcdb3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Finally, a better detector lowers both the floor and the achievable cold. \
Repeat the floor-plus-spread Lyapunov balance at efficiency ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "06331a5a-5e36-eeb4-2fc0-9c045bc0b49e"],
 ", where the conditional covariance sharpens and the gain becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Eta]", "k"}], "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\[CapitalSigma]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23db06c9-5192-a0c1-51f8-9f936024f22b"],
 ", holding ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["G", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7de6255b-dc63-5143-2b9d-bd04d51623a9"],
 " fixed at its ideal-detector value (not re-optimized per ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e05cf72-a918-1ba6-163a-e73fc8ad698c"],
 ", so the cooled curve is conservative at low ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "27233357-6f43-6494-4ed0-ab110af64efe"],
 "):"
}], "Text",
 CellID->559816626,ExpressionUUID->"5de364a1-4a4c-e5c4-0b91-7d0b6ffecf2e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[Eta]_", ",", " ", "gg_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", "[", "\[Eta]", "]"}]}], ",", " ", "kx", ",", 
       " ", "kp", ",", " ", "s"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"kx", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"kp", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"2", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
         RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", "kCool"}], "]"}], " ", 
        RowBox[{"c", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"s", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"LyapunovSolve", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], 
           ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "gammaCool"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ", 
              "gg"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", "^", "2"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"kx", " ", "kp"}], ",", " ", 
              RowBox[{"kp", "^", "2"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
      "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"s", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"c", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", " ",
        "0.5"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[272]:= ",
 CellID->306702529,ExpressionUUID->"691f1a66-023d-d875-1f24-9c40b7c9ab5f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Sweep the efficiency from a poor detector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Eta]", "TI"], "=", "0.2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "338a64d0-666f-51f5-618a-7d9a131a23df"],
 ", to a perfect one:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->660231635,ExpressionUUID->"457416e7-7538-701a-730b-8fc17ccd4360"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"etasCool", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.2", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", "0.01"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[273]:= ",
 CellID->2070365498,ExpressionUUID->"48945f4c-b90a-f7cd-78ac-571638bcdd17"],

Cell["\<\
Plot the conditional floor and the fixed-gain cooled occupation against \
efficiency:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1311299970,ExpressionUUID->"138a5a7b-a86c-a778-418a-5c24c91e0a42"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "+", " ", 
              RowBox[{"#", "[", 
               RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", "-", 
           " ", "0.5"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{"steadyCovCool", " ", "/@", " ", "etasCool"}], ")"}]}]}], 
       "}"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"etasCool", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"nUncCoolEta", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "Gcool"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
         " ", "etasCool"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<conditional floor\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<cooled occupation (fixed gain)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detector efficiency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<phonon number\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<a better detector cools colder\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[274]:= ",
 CellID->1022896615,ExpressionUUID->"508ec8d0-0dfb-c87e-00b5-e19aab8f9b44"],

Cell["\<\
Both curves fall as the detector improves, and the gap between them is the \
price of noisy actuation. This is measurement-based cooling of a \
nanomechanical drum or a levitated nanoparticle toward its ground state, not \
by contact with something colder but by watching precisely and pushing back: \
the same conditional covariance that told the Kalman filter how well it could \
track now sets how cold the feedback can pull.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1963671665,ExpressionUUID->"2a8e75db-4196-2992-5ab6-6c8570237bf8"],

Cell["Part Seven: Two Bookkeepings, and the Colour of the Light", "Section",
 CellID->949858012,ExpressionUUID->"10b44722-1d8a-a843-404c-5e8c943cfaa9"],

Cell["Linear vs Nonlinear: One Trajectory, Two Descriptions", "Subsection",
 CellID->1295537244,ExpressionUUID->"376a42de-a72c-dab7-5d6a-5b9bd2dea89d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " One diffusive history, written under two probability measures. Under a \
reference Wiener measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1e950789-7bdf-2365-46aa-9ed37e6b8e4f"],
 ", the ",
 StyleBox["linear", "TI"],
 " stochastic Schrodinger equation runs an unnormalized state under plain \
noise,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1775107011,ExpressionUUID->"66a9921e-bad7-8e47-0e56-14583f63d4ad"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "=", 
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["(",
       SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
      StyleBox[")",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"-", 
       StyleBox["i", "TI"]}], 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"]}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["1", "2"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
        StyleBox["j", "TI"],
        LimitsPositioning->False], 
       RowBox[{
        SubsuperscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], 
        RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "."}]}]}]}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->1505341139,ExpressionUUID->"17d2ef91-60a0-4e89-3de1-06db115514d3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its squared norm is the Radon-Nikodym likelihood density ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7fb9f494-3700-dcc2-2546-edde42baa628"],
 " of the physical record measure relative to ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43fac4e6-e09d-fa6e-7199-ddc39129c8b4"],
 " up to that time, not an absolute probability for one continuous record. \
Under the physical measure ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["P", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2968eab2-ef34-759a-5f17-03ff8ac15fe0"],
 ", the normalized master equation is driven by the innovation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d87f42e-d652-8147-0bbc-ed8be3e4d3ad"],
 " of the observed increment ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Y", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "556a1f76-4155-b78b-0369-973070e11dd1"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1868278770,ExpressionUUID->"6ae11f47-bcab-5fd1-1a9e-9721355e253b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->False], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
     SubsuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"], "\[Dagger]"], "-", 
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["W", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["v", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "=", 
    RowBox[{"2", "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["Re",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["Tr",
        FontSlant->"Plain"], 
       StyleBox["[",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], 
         StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
        StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
       StyleBox["]",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], "."}]}]}]}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->424354000,ExpressionUUID->"14be3adf-0864-81d7-3c45-b399a916d33d"],

Cell["\<\
The useful fact is that the reference-measure average of the unnormalized \
projectors is the master-equation state. Build the linear version and check.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->532205865,ExpressionUUID->"6fc6e9dd-9955-7f76-15fd-008718e0425c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One diffusive trajectory has two equivalent descriptions. The ",
 StyleBox["nonlinear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SME (used so far) carries the normalized state and renormalizes each step. \
The ",
 StyleBox["linear",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " SSE evolves an unnormalized state under plain (unconditioned) noise, never \
renormalizing,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->512620775,ExpressionUUID->"18ddee5b-7ce8-2fa7-48e2-0005749d758d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[RightAngleBracket]", "=", 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
     FractionBox["1", "2"], 
     SuperscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[RightAngleBracket]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"], "+", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[RightAngleBracket]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["W", "TI"]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->807932579,ExpressionUUID->"1012f954-cdfa-9bde-4021-f111eb8ce924"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "its squared norm ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], ",", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"]}], 
   StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14c14cd5-eb1e-28e1-3cff-659e8eab7acb"],
 " the likelihood ratio ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["P", "TI"], "/", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["Q", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0c226993-d8a3-5fdb-35d1-80dcd9562521"],
 " accumulated by that reference-noise history. The plain ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Q", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "50d2e924-c37a-d2d3-00e1-0081f60ca039"],
 "-average of the unnormalized outer products ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[RightAngleBracket]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"\[LeftBracketingBar]", 
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], "~"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "\[Dagger]"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "790318be-6549-22ff-2f30-91f80cfc70c5"],
 " is the master-equation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3e35e667-42ed-6e5d-67ca-f841769834a7"],
 ". Fix the atom and the non-Hermitian drift ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["K", "TI"], "=", "-", 
   StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["H", "TI"], "^"], "-", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"], "\[Dagger]"], 
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "^"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3d92e0fe-61dd-aa06-6ba1-f9b81069f96c"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->243295841,ExpressionUUID->"55f422cf-5719-5b56-038b-bba962ac29bc"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", " ", "=", " ", "2."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"cLin", " ", "=", " ", "lower"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Knh", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], " ", "-", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cLin", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      "cLin"}], "/", "2"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"step", " ", "=", " ", "0.005"}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"steps", " ", "=", " ", "600"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[275]:= ",
 CellID->416937359,ExpressionUUID->"185882f2-3bbf-8530-4867-1bbcbe4bec1a"],

Cell["One unnormalized run under plain noise, never renormalizing:", "Text",
 CellID->1706026672,ExpressionUUID->"0ec07e75-02a3-3afd-36f0-703fb75788c7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linearRun", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"Fold", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[276]:= ",
 CellID->1235325005,ExpressionUUID->"311eeb5e-e314-7537-6725-031b96a15c1d"],

Cell["Run four hundred of them:", "Text",
 CellID->883233490,ExpressionUUID->"601ed991-4af3-b103-1025-d0db6e870069"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearStates", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linearRun", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[277]:= ",
 CellID->795056725,ExpressionUUID->"27a3aaa2-c993-2819-4d50-430fe8267b63"],

Cell["Average the outer products, with no reweighting at all:", "Text",
 CellID->1402288582,ExpressionUUID->"0a4498bc-a571-157c-3a7b-11f9cc047c46"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Outer", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Times", ",", " ", "#", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
     " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[278]:= ",
 CellID->155652986,ExpressionUUID->"4ce0809c-d5c3-af14-749f-19d9dc77f27e"],

Cell["Measure the gap to the master equation:", "Text",
 CellID->1208643478,ExpressionUUID->"319d38eb-f6c5-3702-67a2-b1b483719a68"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "@", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{"linearAverage", " ", "-", " ", 
     RowBox[{"evolve", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]lin", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "cLin", "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[279]:= ",
 CellID->346146379,ExpressionUUID->"7b2144f6-69f3-9218-2adf-5db00f87e162"],

Cell["\<\
The unweighted reference-measure average matches the master equation within \
Monte-Carlo scatter and Euler time-step error, with no pathwise \
renormalization.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1804730773,ExpressionUUID->"10a6d73c-c2c2-eea0-405d-cf79f774b48a"],

Cell["\<\
The squared norms are likelihood ratios. Their expectation under the \
reference measure is one; the finite seeded Euler sample should be near one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->102052525,ExpressionUUID->"3710847d-4883-61f0-5d2f-1e27693633da"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Mean", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ", 
    "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[280]:= ",
 CellID->1286127511,ExpressionUUID->"4a5dfbae-20e5-2129-7a62-f20850907073"],

Cell["\<\
Different reference-noise histories carry different likelihood-ratio weights.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1085349338,ExpressionUUID->"54fe873c-afbe-d0b8-7c85-1f79ca48a282"],

Cell["Now visualize the distribution of their likelihood weights:", "Text",
 CellID->884952081,ExpressionUUID->"41b5ee91-8ab8-27e2-774a-07db2f328dc8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Histogram", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}], " ",
      "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "linearStates"}], ",", " ", "30", ",", 
   " ", "\"\<PDF\>\"", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<likelihood-ratio weight dP/dQ\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<density\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<reference histories carry likelihood-ratio weights\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[281]:= ",
 CellID->592254278,ExpressionUUID->"033b6291-8419-2638-32d9-7bdb2dad8d02"],

Cell["\<\
These are two descriptions of the same diffusive process related by a change \
of probability measure. Normalize and evolve with the physical innovation to \
get the nonlinear state an experimenter tracks. Evolve the unnormalized state \
under reference Wiener noise to get the linear picture. The linear state's \
direction still fluctuates; its squared norm is the Girsanov/Radon-Nikodym \
factor that converts reference-history averages into physical ones.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1827832951,ExpressionUUID->"69bf3242-ce45-6744-1f44-b42febf04dae"],

Cell["\<\
One record carries both bookkeepings at once. Roll out a single linear run \
keeping its whole history:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1018133995,ExpressionUUID->"34f98250-b9a0-779e-5c86-241a38555de4"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "seed_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"BlockRandom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "seed", "]"}], ";", "\n", "    ", 
     RowBox[{"FoldList", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"#1", " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Knh", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "step"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cLin", " ", ".", " ", "#1"}], " ", "#2"}]}], " ", "&"}], ",",
        " ", "excited", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"RandomVariate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"NormalDistribution", "[", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "step", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", "steps"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"oneA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", "[", "7", "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"gridA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"step", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
     RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "steps"}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[282]:= ",
 CellID->2045666246,ExpressionUUID->"6ff43cc4-be71-93f0-158b-b5ae3b05e1da"],

Cell["\<\
Read the two descriptions off that one run: the normalized state (the state \
direction the physical trajectory takes for this record) and the log-weight \
it accumulates (its likelihood score), on aligned axes:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1382967107,ExpressionUUID->"51b5abc0-0202-0151-074a-42aab7b753bb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
  RowBox[{"{", "\n", "  ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"(", 
               RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
                RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "Z", 
                  " ", ".", " ", "#"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}], " ", 
             "&"}], "[", 
            RowBox[{"Normalize", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", "1.05"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<excited population (normalized)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      
      RowBox[{"PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the state you track\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
    RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"gridA5", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Log", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
             "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "oneA5"}]}], "}"}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
        RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "3"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"steps", " ", "step"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", "All"}], 
        "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "520"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", 
         " ", "\"\<log weight  log ||psi||^2\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{
      "PlotLabel", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<the likelihood it carries\>\""}]}], 
     "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[283]:= ",
 CellID->1417511298,ExpressionUUID->"126b1bc1-46f5-8a3a-4268-92ab7281d900"],

Cell["\<\
The same record has a normalized-state reading and a running weight; neither \
alone is the trajectory, together they are.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1457683890,ExpressionUUID->"046e4336-067c-8bff-2c16-5b70b30ed9c5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The catch of the linear method is that the weights spread, so a handful of \
records come to dominate the average, the importance-sampling degeneracy. \
Measure it with the effective sample size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["N", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eff",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Sum]",
       FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
      StyleBox["w", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "2"], "/", 
   StyleBox["\[Sum]",
    FontSize->1.15 Inherited], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["w", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07815119-4e7f-a41e-2dbf-49436b0b0f64"],
 " across the ensemble over time:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->858004867,ExpressionUUID->"7918a344-d32d-e3ba-2f27-3b21e6d9b180"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essPathsA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"linPathA5", " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "400", "]"}]}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"essA5", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"w", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Re", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", "#"}], 
               "]"}], " ", "&"}], "@", 
             RowBox[{"#", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "j", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", 
          " ", "essPathsA5"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Total", "[", "w", "]"}], "^", "2"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{"Total", "[", 
           RowBox[{"w", "^", "2"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "400."}]}], "]"}], ",",
      " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"j", ",", " ", "1", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"steps", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ",", " ", "20"}], "}"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"gridA5", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", 
        RowBox[{"1", " ", ";;", " ", ";;", " ", "20"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      " ", "essA5"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
     RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<time\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<effective sample size / N\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the linear weights degenerate: fewer records carry the \
average\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[284]:= ",
 CellID->1157433805,ExpressionUUID->"3d8a8157-75dd-89f2-6b89-19117c69dbd8"],

Cell["\<\
The effective fraction falls from one toward a fraction of the ensemble: as \
time goes on, the unweighted linear average is carried by ever fewer \
high-weight records, and its Monte-Carlo error grows even though it remains \
unbiased. That is the price of the linear picture's convenience, and the \
reason the nonlinear (renormalized) equation, which keeps every trajectory \
equally weighted, is what a long real-time filter uses.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->796928914,ExpressionUUID->"280c132e-a962-3439-5833-8a8bc8149f03"],

Cell["The Driven Atom, Averaged and Watched", "Subsection",
 CellID->1009699246,ExpressionUUID->"5c58460f-1f98-22b3-0478-58699a2d7099"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The fully worked driven, damped, emitting atom, both averaged and watched. \
In full generality its unconditional master equation carries detuning, \
thermal drive, and pure dephasing,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1843094008,ExpressionUUID->"0f9d878a-7798-33b0-35a2-1ed40212819a"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[Hacek]"], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox[
      StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "+", "1"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["T", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
     StyleBox["z", "TI"]], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   "\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\[NonBreakingSpace]\
\[NonBreakingSpace]", 
   RowBox[{
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["H", "TI"], "\[Hacek]"], "=", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox[
       RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
        StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}], "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["z", "TI"]]}], "+", 
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}]}]}], ","}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->2053559494,ExpressionUUID->"7e9a25a0-be60-edc7-26b9-bc0a3b1ab72d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "and relaxes to a mixed steady state inside the ball. We take the standard \
resonance-fluorescence corner, resonant (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3456b4ad-9984-7479-5c6d-2df718315f43"],
 "), zero temperature (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   OverscriptBox[
    StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "69d1a328-4310-c880-1fee-3b7276aa9aea"],
 "), no extra dephasing (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1c27efc5-dd5c-0ea0-45dc-06aed4e9548a"],
 "), which reduces it to a single emission channel ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], "^"], "1"], "=", 
   SqrtBox[
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7f9ca573-a525-e7a3-25a3-3d3cccd1cd89"],
 ","
}], "Text",
 CellID->1533578161,ExpressionUUID->"1eda8955-2ca4-ffeb-46f9-211f4556c531"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"\[ScriptCapitalL]", 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], "=", "-", 
    StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      FractionBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
      SubscriptBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], 
       StyleBox["x", "TI"]]}], ",", 
     StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "+", 
    StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "\[ThinSpace]", "\|01d49f", 
    StyleBox["[",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    SubscriptBox[
     OverscriptBox[
      StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
    StyleBox["]",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->876660136,ExpressionUUID->"04eee7d5-a4c3-ea8f-2c95-fe9ecd77b8d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Watching that one channel with unit efficiency keeps the conditioned \
history pure on the surface of the ball; the record-blind average is the \
mixed interior point. Compare the two, then put the general parameters back \
and read the steady state they set. (Detuning ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", 
   StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2fb07358-8f92-ce5d-5540-6b022a2494a7"],
 " is a Hamiltonian term: it turns the conditioned trajectory but never mixes \
it. Temperature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  OverscriptBox[
   StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "18c8dd31-1ea6-1036-48f7-d57b9b53631c"],
 " and extra dephasing ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "154dc22c-e6d4-21a3-4372-db8993617389"],
 " add channels that do mix the trajectory, but only when their output goes \
unrecorded; monitor every channel ideally and even they leave it pure.)"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1974583224,ExpressionUUID->"00023c2b-283d-9017-3031-b67549c9e37d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Before specializing, solve the general steady state once, so the corner we \
pick is a corner of something actually worked. Two rates organize it: the \
longitudinal rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "495d6937-f906-8dd0-7f62-8170f8b0d73a"],
 " at which populations relax, and the transverse rate ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"], "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "+", "2", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d937789-2253-fc97-1ba1-6ed357e7c6fd"],
 " at which coherences decay, faster than ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "1"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "579a3a64-9432-ab70-7db9-bc4e1dc4f65a"],
 " by the extra dephasing. Define the steady Bloch vector in closed form:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->761010835,ExpressionUUID->"194a91b0-0c16-7c4e-4f49-08faa5a34694"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalDelta]_", ",", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",",
      " ", "nT_", ",", " ", "kd_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"G1", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"2", " ", "nT"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}]}], ",", 
       " ", 
       RowBox[{"G2", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"2", " ", "nT"}], " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
           "2"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{"2", " ", "\[Gamma]", " ", "kd"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
     "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"den", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"G1", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"G2", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
          
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "^", "2"}], " ", "G2"}]}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", "\[CapitalOmega]", " ", 
           "\[CapitalDelta]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"\[Gamma]", " ", "\[CapitalOmega]", " ", "G2"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "\[Gamma]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"G2", "^", "2"}], " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalDelta]", "^", "2"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}], "/", 
        "den"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[285]:= ",
 CellID->1273215491,ExpressionUUID->"1e65ff1b-2e7b-83a1-461a-f7454b0fd18b"],

Cell["\<\
Check it against the toolkit's steady-state finder with detuning, \
temperature, and dephasing all switched on:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1918360181,ExpressionUUID->"2949918d-6dca-6327-5f76-08d7047f4e0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
     RowBox[{
     "1.3", ",", " ", "3.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.4", ",", " ", 
      "0.25"}], "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
     RowBox[{"First", "@", 
      RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1.3", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "Z"}], " ", "+", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"3.", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}]}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", 
             RowBox[{"(", 
              RowBox[{"0.4", " ", "+", " ", "1"}], ")"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
           "lower"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", "0.4"}], "]"}], " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "lower", "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
            RowBox[{"1.", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}], " ", "Z"}]}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[286]:= ",
 CellID->905478106,ExpressionUUID->"2fb7f3c1-5a6e-58a9-554c-eaab5f1b2af3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The discrepancy is at numerical precision: the closed form is exact for the \
stated finite-dimensional Bloch equations. The detuning enters through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubsuperscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2", "2"], "+", "\[CapitalDelta]", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Omega]", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "168bc571-ef41-c55f-3e88-dd3a8af5afa5"],
 " in the denominator, so the resonance has a Lorentzian denominator of width \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f736822-19f9-ab87-4500-818c9f8df9ed"],
 " that the drive power-broadens through the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   SubscriptBox["\[CapitalGamma]", "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "287634d7-a493-5377-580d-ad90cd263e5d"],
 " term; temperature lifts the ground-state bias, since at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "31701ca2-f4c0-d723-670f-950ffd7aba09"],
 " the state rests at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["z", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["eq",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]], "=", "-", "1", "/", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"2", 
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["n", "TI"], "_"], "+", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "42383645-cae2-5342-73c7-a82eee9721a8"],
 " rather than the south pole. Plot the steady excited population ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"1", "+", 
    StyleBox["z", "TI"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b11b9e5-bb8f-782a-392e-30cf3e3a4b70"],
 " against detuning, weak drive against strong:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1698065530,ExpressionUUID->"49614dfc-87d5-9726-7f1f-64a63261fa0c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"steadyGeneral", "[", 
              RowBox[{
              "d", ",", " ", "om", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", 
               "0."}], "]"}], "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "3", "]"}], "]"}]}], ")"}], "/", "2"}]}], "}"}], ",",
        " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"d", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"-", "8"}], ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "}"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1.", ",", " ", "4."}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<\[CapitalOmega] = 1\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<\[CapitalOmega] = 4\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", "Automatic"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<detuning \[CapitalDelta]\[Omega]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<steady excited population\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<resonance is a power-broadened Lorentzian in detuning\>\""}]}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[287]:= ",
 CellID->149360148,ExpressionUUID->"4eaeef1c-70dd-f5e5-7655-07460169dfcf"],

Cell["\<\
The excited population peaks on resonance and falls off as a Lorentzian to \
either side; the stronger drive both lifts the peak toward saturation at one \
half and widens it, the power broadening. That is the general averaged atom. \
For the watched picture we now take the cleanest corner of it, where a single \
monitored channel keeps the record pure.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->990508151,ExpressionUUID->"5ab084b1-712e-e46c-0a4f-1dfb00d8ceb6"],

Cell["\<\
Pull the threads together on one worked example: a driven, emitting atom. \
Averaged (unconditioned), it relaxes to a mixed steady state inside the Bloch \
ball. Fix the atom and compute its steady Bloch vector:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->472375463,ExpressionUUID->"009434ca-e8a5-36b3-30ab-ad9789519c99"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", " ", "=", " ", "3."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"\[Gamma]dr", " ", "=", " ", "1."}], ";", " ", 
  RowBox[{"settled", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", 
    RowBox[{"First", "@", 
     RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", "/", "2"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]dr", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
      "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[288]:= ",
 CellID->1352706751,ExpressionUUID->"2a229ce6-e7c6-f6b5-5bd1-15c39270dc9f"],

Cell["Read its length (a pure state has length one):", "Text",
 CellID->890986319,ExpressionUUID->"56ef6f30-06fe-ca48-7e94-877ab2889892"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "settled", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[289]:= ",
 CellID->1572592159,ExpressionUUID->"3d7e8caf-dec1-3276-6b05-2508db75815c"],

Cell["\<\
The length is well short of one: the averaged state is mixed.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->523613550,ExpressionUUID->"2a4b2e91-3e68-2f67-5a48-c7dbbb1d724d"],

Cell["\<\
But a conditioned trajectory, keeping the record, stays pure on the surface \
of the ball, fluctuating around that mixed average. Run one:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->506908930,ExpressionUUID->"2e070ed5-18e9-e926-563c-a79f989db80c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"watched", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"trajectory", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"densityMatrix", "[", "excited", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]dr", "/", "2"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]dr", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}], ",", 
     " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "1.", "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", " ", "0.01", ",", " ", "8.", ",", " ", "5"}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[290]:= ",
 CellID->783859841,ExpressionUUID->"7866ed4e-196e-bd16-281d-05289818047c"],

Cell["\<\
Confirm it stays pure, reading the largest linear entropy along the whole run:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->836234808,ExpressionUUID->"5d58b19a-61e1-4a53-0b67-28c4179418b9"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "-", " ", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Norm", "[", 
         RowBox[{"blochVector", "[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], ")"}], "/",
      "2"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   RowBox[{"watched", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[291]:= ",
 CellID->410625993,ExpressionUUID->"039e17dc-7135-1c98-31a5-8e8600c066e2"],

Cell["\<\
The largest linear entropy stays at zero within numerical precision.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->230379626,ExpressionUUID->"76f331b0-e4d2-d206-1e80-a8fd8d64a16c"],

Cell["\<\
Now visualize the pure trajectory on the Bloch-sphere surface, with the mixed \
averaged state marked inside:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->26532680,ExpressionUUID->"5aa658dd-12e3-7f58-0a5e-5187a69645a2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"blochPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"blochVector", " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"watched", "[", "\"\<states\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   " ", "\"\<a pure trajectory circles the mixed average (black dot)\>\"", ",",
    " ", "None", ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"Black", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PointSize", "[", "0.035", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Point", "[", "settled", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[292]:= ",
 CellID->1009717036,ExpressionUUID->"25a3641b-c972-205a-5351-7e44e80772a0"],

Cell["\<\
The surface path is the atom as an observer with the complete ideal record \
sees it; the interior point is the atom after that record is averaged out. \
Neither is more true; they answer different questions. The contrast applies \
whenever the initial state is pure, every decohering channel is monitored, \
and efficiency is one; examples with missed or thermal channels correctly \
produce mixed conditioned states.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->151019001,ExpressionUUID->"0d85d5e7-830f-4689-3bba-ccc136ba2cd3"],

Cell["The Mollow Triplet: Resonance-Fluorescence Spectrum", "Subsection",
 CellID->1656643860,ExpressionUUID->"06d28d0f-e448-85b2-2ee1-25688de2ef98"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["The problem.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The spectrum (power spectrum) of the light a driven atom emits, computed \
by quantum regression from the master equation's two-time correlations. The \
light divides into two parts: an ",
 StyleBox["elastic", "TI"],
 " (coherent) line at the drive frequency, a delta function carrying the \
weight ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SuperscriptBox[GridBox[{
     {
      SubscriptBox[
       RowBox[{
        StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1], 
        SubscriptBox[
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
        StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
         SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
       StyleBox["ss",
        FontSlant->"Plain"]]}
    },
    GridBoxDividers->{"Columns" -> {True, True}, "Rows" -> {}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{0.15}}}], "2"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "51b905fb-db49-ff7a-0746-9ca4defdc240"],
 ", and the ",
 StyleBox["inelastic", "TI"],
 " (fluorescence) spectrum of the fluctuations ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], "-", 
   SubscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     SubscriptBox[
      OverscriptBox[
       StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
     StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    StyleBox["ss",
     FontSlant->"Plain"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1f015443-b004-ded7-453f-4e2cc1b6a43d"],
 ", which by quantum regression is a resolvent of the Liouvillian at the \
steady state,"
}], "Text",
 CellID->24370237,ExpressionUUID->"79dc6473-7f99-4552-2fe4-7e3d7a2c2fb8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 PaneBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["inel",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], 
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1], "\[Proportional]", 
    StyleBox["Re",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    SubsuperscriptBox["\[Integral]", "0", "\[Infinity]"], 
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
     RowBox[{"-", 
      StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["t", "TI"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[LeftAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1], 
      RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], 
       StyleBox["t", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "\[ThinSpace]", 
       StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
       StyleBox["(",
        SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
       StyleBox[")",
        SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
      StyleBox["\[RightAngleBracket]",
       SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
     StyleBox["ss",
      FontSlant->"Plain"]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["t", "TI"]}], "."}],
  Alignment->Center,
  ImageSize->Full]], "DisplayFormula",
 CellID->730383262,ExpressionUUID->"74d8dc7d-61a6-0fac-1ce7-d627105355f6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "For weak driving the inelastic part is a single line; for strong driving ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ">", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "254b6ea2-640f-5114-5348-870c0dba207e"],
 " it splits into the three-peaked ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet", "TI"],
 ", a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4a37b9ca-0c89-88bb-7bcc-3094a53dda81"],
 ", the dynamical Stark effect."
}], "Text",
 CellID->304869518,ExpressionUUID->"57618033-75bd-c863-7d1e-1a7d7c499b49"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Homodyne detection instead reads a chosen quadrature, and its spectrum can \
dip ",
 StyleBox["below", "TI"],
 " the shot-noise floor: squeezed, nonclassical light. Build both from the \
same big matrix."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1481638679,ExpressionUUID->"1b228fec-7489-5fb6-4ad1-26b67d3c259c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "One last set of quantities from the master equation, all through the \
eigen-based spectrum tool built for the quantum point contact (",
 Cell[BoxData["regressionSpectrum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15cf7838-770d-10a7-43f5-726202b8628d"],
 "). It needs no shifted frequency grid, because the steady mode is dropped \
explicitly. The inelastic fluorescence spectrum is its correlation of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Delta]", "TI"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0b95bd50-7b57-adaf-39aa-351a7ee3f7f5"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1624629187,ExpressionUUID->"216b1f6b-5cec-53ab-5768-9735549921f1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
    RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "tones_"}], 
    "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}], ",",
           " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "    ", 
       RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{"First", "@", 
         RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"(", 
             RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
           " ", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
          "]"}]}]}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{"With", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"dm", " ", "=", " ", 
         RowBox[{"lower", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
            RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], " ", "id2"}]}]}], 
        "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"regressionSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"dm", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "dm", "]"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], 
        "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[293]:= ",
 CellID->251976942,ExpressionUUID->"16ee990f-09f0-daa5-3e95-1169af8aa88f"],

Cell["\<\
Sweep frequencies (centered on zero, no offset needed) for a weak and a \
strong drive:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1001631779,ExpressionUUID->"00067b34-c3cd-1811-303e-7371f6786b7b"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tones", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"-", "9"}], ",", " ", "9", ",", " ", "0.05"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"weak", ",", " ", "strong"}], "}"}], " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"0.6", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
      RowBox[{"6.", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[294]:= ",
 CellID->131866538,ExpressionUUID->"2db117d6-0b72-000c-5b4e-8e90ae075356"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Weakly driven, the inelastic spectrum is a single line at the drive \
frequency. Strongly driven, it splits into the ",
 StyleBox["Mollow triplet",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ": a central line and two sidebands at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68a1b4b4-f7f8-1850-185e-2df1818d6aba"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2120574329,ExpressionUUID->"666da514-18bd-d59b-0e12-3d5e9949bfe1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Now visualize the weak- and strong-drive inelastic spectra together. Their \
absolute scales differ by orders of magnitude (the weak line would vanish on \
the strong axis), so plot each normalized to its own peak to compare the ",
 StyleBox["shapes", "TI"],
 ", a single line against the triplet:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->905900721,ExpressionUUID->"29592712-3b20-e448-5f66-bf5cbedace92"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"weak", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "weak", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"strong", "/", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", "strong", "]"}]}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "6"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "6"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      "None"}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<weak drive\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<strong drive\>\""}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency (relative to drive)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<inelastic spectrum (each / its peak)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<strong driving splits the inelastic spectrum into the Mollow \
triplet\>\""}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[295]:= ",
 CellID->30454613,ExpressionUUID->"22115567-c1d8-2747-522f-4d40f0528dad"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The sidebands sit near ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6b71a00b-a0b6-756c-190e-3a54d1435fb6"],
 ": under strong driving the atom's levels are dressed into a four-level \
ladder, whose transitions produce the three lines. Confirm the sidebands land \
at the drive strength:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->936073442,ExpressionUUID->"79f35eab-5065-8c8a-2f81-57f56111d6d0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"tones", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "#", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"FindPeaks", "[", "strong", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"[", 
      RowBox[{"All", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Abs", "[", "#", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", "6"}], "]"}], " ", "<", 
     " ", "0.6"}], " ", "&"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[296]:= ",
 CellID->2004769691,ExpressionUUID->"6cbd088d-a6f8-eb62-1442-a1d6d372b648"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The peaks sit at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "71854dcf-cc44-2a9b-27bb-64a8e5f178e1"],
 ". Confirm too that the inelastic spectrum is nowhere negative, as a genuine \
power spectrum must be:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1569231351,ExpressionUUID->"412c5b26-c47d-b90f-70d4-5283ed090855"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", "strong", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[297]:= ",
 CellID->1612045584,ExpressionUUID->"5f352ef2-4ae2-2c59-06ca-c7bc6e9776a3"],

Cell["Nonnegative within numerical precision.", "Text",
 CellID->1224848414,ExpressionUUID->"0d7f7a51-5ff5-70fd-3b05-7c1b598042c7"],

Cell["\<\
The elastic line lives separately, a delta at zero frequency whose weight is \
the coherent dipole; it dominates at weak drive and all but vanishes at \
strong drive as the light turns fully inelastic:\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->152101747,ExpressionUUID->"3089d968-2504-f1ea-60b6-d1324cb6c330"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "\[CapitalOmega]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"With", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "1.", "]"}], " ", "lower"}], "}"}]}], 
         "]"}]}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
       RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
        RowBox[{"lower", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}], "]"}], "^", "2"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "0.6", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"elasticWeight", "[", "6.", "]"}]}], "}"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[298]:= ",
 CellID->1101372283,ExpressionUUID->"2b65a66f-d41b-de4c-591a-3848ddafa496"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The coherent weight falls by more than an order of magnitude from weak to \
strong drive. To watch the triplet being born, sweep the drive continuously \
and stack the inelastic spectra into a heatmap. The central peak dwarfs the \
sidebands at every drive, so scale each row to its own peak to keep the \
sidebands visible, and overlay the dressed-transition lines ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "428af588-0a0e-1d2d-7289-ecd2afbb6477"],
 " as guides:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->137398679,ExpressionUUID->"64da9960-6030-4ffa-0cf9-114a11c515c0"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowDrives", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
    RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "8", ",", " ", "0.25"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"#", "/", 
       RowBox[{"Max", "[", "#", "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"mollowInelastic", "[", 
        RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Range", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "11"}], ",", " ", "11", ",", " ", "0.1"}], "]"}]}], 
        "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", "mollowDrives"}], ")"}]}]}], 
  ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ArrayPlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHeat", ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"-", "11"}], ",", " ", "11"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"First", "@", "mollowDrives"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Last", "@", "mollowDrives"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"DataReversed", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ColorFunction", " ", "->", " ", "\"\<SunsetColors\>\""}], ",", 
   " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"AspectRatio", " ", "->", " ", "1.1"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "460"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Epilog", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
       RowBox[{"White", ",", " ", "Dashed", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Opacity", "[", "0.7", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"0.3", ",", " ", "0.3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"8", ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Line", "[", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "0.3"}], ",", " ", "0.3"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"-", "8"}], ",", " ", "8"}], "}"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<drive \[CapitalOmega]\>\""}],
      "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the Mollow triplet is born as the drive grows (rows scaled to \
peak; \[Mu]=\[PlusMinus]\[CapitalOmega] dashed)\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[299]:= ",
 CellID->1953556957,ExpressionUUID->"6c687fea-7568-041a-1468-76b47c1d6f60"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The bright ridge splits into three, the outer two fanning apart along ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Mu]", "TI"], "=", "\[PlusMinus]", "\[CapitalOmega]"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0cbccda1-a060-0aa2-3443-e40ad1155888"],
 ": the dressed-state sidebands. The triplet is what an ordinary spectrometer \
sees."
}], "Text",
 CellID->943903693,ExpressionUUID->"447fe503-da77-e068-6c04-fd6cdf03b2b2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A homodyne detector sees something an intensity spectrometer cannot: it \
measures one quadrature ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "-"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
     StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"]}]], "+", 
   SubscriptBox[
    OverscriptBox[
     StyleBox["\[Sigma]", "TI"], "^"], "+"], 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["e", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"i", "\[Theta]"}], "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "708a530c-476f-43a5-208a-4b56721a118f"],
 ", and its spectrum, normalized so the shot-noise floor is one, can fall \
below that floor. The weak drive we examine, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c4be775-fc25-beb3-2448-ff3ef5d10499"],
 ", is exactly an exceptional point of this Liouvillian, the same coalescence \
the quantum point contact met: its two dressed modes merge there, so we read \
this spectrum with the mode-free ",
 Cell[BoxData["resolventSpectrum"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "144f2f1f-85ce-1d43-3c74-c7592c7b67a9"],
 " rather than the eigenmode sum, which would divide by a singular \
eigenbasis. Build it from the measurement current fluctuations:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->292818558,ExpressionUUID->"6c6a609e-b44f-cf74-146a-79d83dfb925e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[CapitalOmega]_", ",", " ", "\[Gamma]_", ",", " ", "\[Theta]_", ",", 
     " ", "tones_"}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Module", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"c", " ", "=", " ", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", "\[Gamma]", "]"}], " ", "lower"}]}], ",", " ", 
       "big", ",", " ", "rss", ",", " ", "cth", ",", " ", "mq", ",", " ", 
       "mean"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"big", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"liouvillian", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}], ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"rss", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"First", "@", 
        RowBox[{"steadyState", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "/", "2"}], ")"}], " ", "X"}], ",", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"{", "c", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"cth", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"c", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Exp", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"-", "I"}], " ", "\[Theta]"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mq", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cth", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}]}], ";", " ", 
      RowBox[{"mean", " ", "=", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Re", "@", 
        RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], "]"}]}]}], ";", "\n", "   ", 
      RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
       RowBox[{"resolventSpectrum", "[", 
        RowBox[{"big", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"cth", " ", ".", " ", "rss"}], " ", "+", " ", 
          RowBox[{"rss", " ", ".", " ", 
           RowBox[{"ConjugateTranspose", "[", "cth", "]"}]}], " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "rss"}]}], ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"mq", " ", "-", " ", 
          RowBox[{"mean", " ", "id2"}]}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}]}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[300]:= ",
 CellID->264739147,ExpressionUUID->"25b14c23-2eb1-df26-534f-658d4b45a20c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "At weak drive, one quadrature is squeezed and the perpendicular one is not. \
Compare the two at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", "0.25", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "008546a0-c650-abb4-30bb-5f0df3eaf99e"],
 ":"
}], "Text",
 CellID->1237098126,ExpressionUUID->"25dc0687-8bfe-aded-53e3-9fe12d88f737"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"tones", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
         RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", "0.", ",", " ", "tones"}], 
         "]"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotStyle", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "1"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"ColorData", "[", 
       RowBox[{"97", ",", " ", "2"}], "]"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"None", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotLegends", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<squeezed quadrature (\[Theta] = \[Pi]/2)\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<anti-squeezed (\[Theta] = 0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"0.7", ",", " ", "All"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ImageSize", " ", "->", " ", "560"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<frequency\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<homodyne spectrum / shot noise\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<resonance fluorescence dips below the shot-noise floor\>\""}]}],
   "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[301]:= ",
 CellID->294194286,ExpressionUUID->"39ea782b-3727-74ef-6fea-727542d25e35"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Theta]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0337beb4-3f4a-26a7-32cc-37febafc8c8d"],
 " quadrature dips below the dashed shot-noise line while its partner rises \
above it: the atom's fluorescence is squeezed, its noise pushed below the \
vacuum in one quadrature at the cost of excess in the other. Confirm the dip \
is real:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->757102330,ExpressionUUID->"19027a34-c886-4faa-4f32-7c71e93315f0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
  RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
   RowBox[{"0.25", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", "tones"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[302]:= ",
 CellID->296089063,ExpressionUUID->"3a07d01d-1b7c-2a0f-6a3c-ca479e097955"],

Cell["\<\
Below one: sub-shot-noise, a signature of nonclassical light that only \
phase-sensitive (homodyne) detection can reveal, and that the \
necessarily-nonnegative intensity spectrum of the triplet can never show.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1606580443,ExpressionUUID->"27ef5936-9de9-9a7d-4d95-51701b9de947"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "How far the squeezing reaches, and where it is deepest, is a question about \
the drive, and it is cleanest at zero frequency, the bottom of the dip we \
just drew. There the homodyne spectrum has the closed form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", "1", "+", "8", 
   SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"4", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"], "-", "1"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{"1", "+", "2", 
      SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalOmega]", "2"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], "3"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "61b66095-ece2-945e-174e-79de8494fea4"],
 " in units of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d61acce-ca29-858f-0b1e-45abefddefd5"],
 ", which drops below one exactly when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "<", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337dac42-7f47-0b68-6102-462c7af259b2"],
 ". Read ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b31e76a-9cc9-3dd2-6ace-ff34157d8738"],
 " off the same machinery across the drive:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->2086732509,ExpressionUUID->"0462e13d-5914-5391-2c11-f96758a121fb"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "\[CapitalOmega]_", "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"mollowHom", "[", 
     RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", ",", " ", "1.", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "2"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "0.", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", 
    RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"ListLinePlot", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "om", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", "0.05", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.02"}], 
      "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Frame", " ", "->", " ", "True"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"GridLines", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", "0.5", "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Directive", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Gray", ",", " ", "Dashed"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], "}"}]}], 
     "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PlotRange", " ", "->", " ", "All"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   RowBox[{"FrameLabel", " ", "->", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<drive \[CapitalOmega]/\[Gamma]\>\"", ",", 
      " ", "\"\<zero-frequency spectrum S(0)\>\""}], "}"}]}], ",", "\n", " ", 
   
   RowBox[{
   "PlotLabel", " ", "->", 
    " ", "\"\<the in-phase quadrature is squeezed only for \[CapitalOmega] < \
\[Gamma]/2\>\""}]}], "]"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[303]:= ",
 CellID->1259953946,ExpressionUUID->"5fafb436-a125-8572-0554-2e73d0d1ec58"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "0", 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5937c2c5-33c1-e073-08cc-dbaf4675b359"],
 " dips below the shot-noise line on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "<", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f5c2ef4-7109-f5b8-3563-c7be00bddf82"],
 " (the vertical gridline) and rises above it past that drive, deepest at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"\[CapitalOmega]", "=", 
   FractionBox["1", "2"], 
   SqrtBox[
    RowBox[{"3", "-", 
     SqrtBox["7"]}]], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Gamma]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "249f21f6-b74e-bacc-4ca4-b8b3c2f80816"],
 ", where it reaches ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"323", "-", "56", 
    SqrtBox["7"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "/", "243"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d7028df-510c-978f-1b0f-c19960befdd5"],
 ". Push harder and the anti-squeezed quadrature's excess noise floods over \
the floor: the in-phase squeezing is a weak-drive effect, and the shallow \
spectral squeezing that lingers to higher drive has slid off zero frequency. \
Confirm the plotted curve is that closed form and not an artifact of the \
resolvent:"
}], "Text",
 CellID->544170496,ExpressionUUID->"67e8013d-d0f3-07d6-0d97-9966e0866d3c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Max", "@", 
  RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"zeroFreqSqueeze", "[", "om", "]"}], " ", "-", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
        RowBox[{"8", " ", 
         RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}], " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"4", " ", 
             RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}], " ", "-", " ", "1"}], ")"}], "/", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", " ", "+", " ", 
             RowBox[{"2", " ", 
              RowBox[{"om", "^", "2"}]}]}], ")"}], "^", "3"}]}]}]}], ")"}]}], 
     "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"om", ",", " ", "0.05", ",", " ", "1.2", ",", " ", "0.05"}], 
     "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[304]:= ",
 CellID->186431800,ExpressionUUID->"2aeb0016-a16b-917c-5ae8-9a53d01fe046"],

Cell["\<\
The maximum discrepancy is at numerical precision. The whole spectroscopy, \
elastic line, inelastic triplet, and squeezing dip, comes from the two-time \
correlations of the same master equation built on the first page.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->480122852,ExpressionUUID->"6e2a9277-acfe-a475-1629-1430c4880f5f"],

Cell["Where This Leaves Us", "Section",
 CellID->1734463933,ExpressionUUID->"7757f304-1d73-ea00-1d6c-eb6e9407b96a"],

Cell["\<\
From plain matrices and a few rules, we built a small laboratory for open \
quantum systems: the master equation for the unconditioned average, a \
positivity-preserving finite-step filter for a kept record, and plotters for \
the Bloch sphere, phase space, covariance ellipses, and spectra. On that \
base, twenty systems: pure dephasing, a driven damped atom, a cavity cat \
decohering at a rate set by the square of its separation, the Haroche \
experiment, dispersive qubit readout, quantum Brownian motion, the \
jump/homodyne/heterodyne unravellings, the quantum Zeno effect, a charge \
qubit read by a quantum point contact, measurement-induced collapse, a \
quantum Kalman filter, measurement feedback, thermalization, rapid \
purification, feedback cooling, the linear-vs-nonlinear trajectory, and the \
Mollow triplet. The recurring theme is conditionality: a complete ideal \
record can keep an initially pure state on a pure stochastic trajectory, \
whereas missed channels, inefficiency, or mixed initial data produce mixed \
conditional states. In every unravelling, ensemble recovery of the master \
equation is a joint large-sample and small-step limit. Change a number, rerun \
the convergence checks, and watch the physics move.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1234622209,ExpressionUUID->"3fa4a1ef-0881-bd46-655b-38c9a93507ac"]
},
